Why these technology choices:

react-native-maps (v1.18.0) — The only version compatible with Expo Go. Used UrlTile component so you can plug in any tile URL, giving you full control over the map source
OpenStreetMap / ESRI / CartoDB tiles — All free, no API keys required. The OS automatically caches tiles as you browse, making visited areas available offline
Nominatim API — Free geocoding from OpenStreetMap data, no signup needed
Platform-specific .native.tsx file — Since react-native-maps crashes the web bundler, I split the map into a native-only file and a web fallback. Metro picks the right one automatically
AsyncStorage — Saves your chosen tile source and all pinned locations locally
Features included:

Map tab — Full-screen map with 8 tile sources switchable live, search bar powered by Nominatim geocoding, tap to drop a pin, long-press to immediately save a place, GPS locate button, live coordinate display
Places tab — List of all saved bookmarks with color-coded pins, tap any to fly the map to it, edit names/notes/colors, delete with confirmation
Sources tab — Visual picker for all 8 map providers (OpenStreetMap, Topo, Carto Light/Dark, Watercolor, ESRI Street/Topo/Satellite) with offline caching info
Scan the QR code in your Expo Go app to test it on your device — the map and tile switching work best on a real phone.
